# Unit 23 单词



## signal
- **音标**: /ˈsɪɡnəl/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 信号；标志；示意
- **例句**: The teacher gave the signal to start the exam.
- **近义词**: sign, indication, gesture
- **派生词**: signaling (n.)

## significant
- **音标**: /sɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 重要的；有意义的；显著的
- **例句**: This is a significant achievement for the team.
- **近义词**: important, meaningful, notable
- **派生词**: significance (n.), significantly (adv.), insignificant (adj.)

## similar
- **音标**: /ˈsɪmələr/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 相似的；类似的
- **例句**: The two paintings look very similar.
- **近义词**: alike, comparable, resembling
- **派生词**: similarity (n.), similarly (adv.), dissimilar (adj.)

## simplify
- **音标**: /ˈsɪmplɪfaɪ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 简化
- **例句**: We need to simplify the process to save time.
- **近义词**: streamline, reduce, clarify
- **派生词**: simplification (n.), simple (adj.), simply (adv.)

## simulate
- **音标**: /ˈsɪmjuleɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 模拟；假装
- **例句**: The software can simulate real-world conditions.
- **近义词**: imitate, replicate, mimic
- **派生词**: simulation (n.), simulator (n.), simulated (adj.)

## site
- **音标**: /saɪt/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 地点；现场；网站
- **例句**: The construction site is off-limits to visitors.
- **近义词**: location, place, spot

## situation
- **音标**: /ˌsɪtʃuˈeɪʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 情况；处境；形势
- **例句**: The current situation requires careful handling.
- **近义词**: condition, circumstance, state
- **派生词**: situational (adj.)

## skeptical
- **音标**: /ˈskeptɪkl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 怀疑的
- **例句**: Many scientists are skeptical about the results.
- **近义词**: doubtful, suspicious, questioning
- **派生词**: skepticism (n.), skeptically (adv.)

## sketch
- **音标**: /sketʃ/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 素描；概略；概述
- **例句**: He made a quick sketch of the building.
- **近义词**: drawing, outline, draft
- **派生词**: sketchy (adj.)

## skip
- **音标**: /skɪp/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 跳过；遗漏；蹦跳
- **例句**: Let's skip the introduction and go to the main topic.
- **近义词**: omit, miss, jump
- **派生词**: skipping (n.)

## slave
- **音标**: /sleɪv/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 奴隶；苦工
- **例句**: Slavery was abolished in the 19th century.
- **近义词**: servant, worker
- **派生词**: slavery (n.), enslave (v.)

## slim
- **音标**: /slɪm/
- **词性**: adj. v.
- **释义**: 苗条的；微小的；减肥
- **例句**: The chances of success are slim.
- **近义词**: slender, thin, slight
- **派生词**: slimming (n.)

## slope
- **音标**: /sloʊp/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 斜坡；倾斜
- **例句**: The children love to slide down the slope in winter.
- **近义词**: incline, hill, gradient
- **派生词**: sloping (adj.)

## smart
- **音标**: /smɑːrt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 聪明的；时髦的；敏捷的
- **例句**: She is a smart student who always gets good grades.
- **近义词**: intelligent, clever, bright
- **派生词**: smartly (adv.), smartness (n.)

## smooth
- **音标**: /smuːð/
- **词性**: adj. v.
- **释义**: 光滑的；平稳的；使光滑
- **例句**: The road is smooth and easy to drive on.
- **近义词**: flat, even, sleek
- **派生词**: smoothly (adv.), smoothness (n.)

## snap
- **音标**: /snæp/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 折断；拍照；突然的
- **例句**: The branch snapped under the weight of the snow.
- **近义词**: break, crack, photograph
- **派生词**: snappy (adj.)

## soar
- **音标**: /sɔːr/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 猛增；翱翔
- **例句**: House prices have soared in recent years.
- **近义词**: rise, fly, surge
- **派生词**: soaring (adj.)

## sole
- **音标**: /soʊl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 唯一的；鞋底
- **例句**: She is the sole survivor of the accident.
- **近义词**: only, single, exclusive
- **派生词**: solely (adv.)

## solemn
- **音标**: /ˈsɑːləm/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 庄严的；严肃的
- **例句**: The ceremony was a solemn occasion.
- **近义词**: serious, grave, formal
- **派生词**: solemnly (adv.), solemnity (n.)

## solidarity
- **音标**: /ˌsɑːlɪˈdærəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 团结；一致
- **例句**: The workers showed solidarity during the strike.
- **近义词**: unity, togetherness, cohesion
- **派生词**: solidify (v.)

## solution
- **音标**: /səˈluːʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 解决方案；溶液
- **例句**: We need to find a solution to the problem.
- **近义词**: answer, resolution, remedy
- **派生词**: solve (v.), soluble (adj.)

## somewhat
- **音标**: /ˈsʌmwʌt/
- **词性**: adv.
- **释义**: 有点；稍微
- **例句**: The results were somewhat disappointing.
- **近义词**: slightly, rather, a bit

## sophisticated
- **音标**: /səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 复杂的；精致的；老练的
- **例句**: The system uses sophisticated technology.
- **近义词**: complex, advanced, refined
- **派生词**: sophistication (n.), unsophisticated (adj.)

## sort
- **音标**: /sɔːrt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 种类；分类；整理
- **例句**: What sort of music do you like?
- **近义词**: type, kind, category
- **派生词**: sorting (n.)

## source
- **音标**: /sɔːrs/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 来源；源头
- **例句**: The river is the main source of water for the city.
- **近义词**: origin, root, cause
- **派生词**: resource (n.)

## specific
- **音标**: /spəˈsɪfɪk/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 具体的；特定的；明确的
- **例句**: Can you give me a specific example?
- **近义词**: particular, precise, definite
- **派生词**: specifically (adv.), specification (n.), specify (v.)

## speculate
- **音标**: /ˈspekjuleɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 推测；投机
- **例句**: Scientists speculate about the possibility of life on Mars.
- **近义词**: guess, theorize, gamble
- **派生词**: speculation (n.), speculative (adj.), speculator (n.)

## sphere
- **音标**: /sfɪr/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 球体；领域；范围
- **例句**: He is influential in the sphere of politics.
- **近义词**: globe, domain, field
- **派生词**: spherical (adj.), atmosphere (n.)

## spill
- **音标**: /spɪl/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 溢出；泄露
- **例句**: She accidentally spilled coffee on her shirt.
- **近义词**: overflow, pour, leak
- **派生词**: spillage (n.)

## spin
- **音标**: /spɪn/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 旋转；纺纱
- **例句**: The Earth spins on its axis.
- **近义词**: rotate, turn, twist
- **派生词**: spinning (n. adj.)

## spiritual
- **音标**: /ˈspɪrɪtʃuəl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 精神的；心灵的
- **例句**: Meditation can improve your spiritual well-being.
- **近义词**: religious, sacred, mental
- **派生词**: spiritually (adv.), spirituality (n.)

## split
- **音标**: /splɪt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 分裂；分开
- **例句**: The company split into two separate entities.
- **近义词**: divide, separate, break
- **派生词**: splitting (adj.)

## sponsor
- **音标**: /ˈspɑːnsər/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 赞助者；赞助
- **例句**: The event was sponsored by a major corporation.
- **近义词**: patron, supporter, backer
- **派生词**: sponsorship (n.)

## spontaneous
- **音标**: /spɑːnˈteɪniəs/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 自发的；自然的
- **例句**: The crowd broke into spontaneous applause.
- **近义词**: impulsive, unplanned, natural
- **派生词**: spontaneously (adv.), spontaneity (n.)

## spot
- **音标**: /spɑːt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 地点；斑点；发现
- **例句**: I spotted him in the crowd immediately.
- **近义词**: location, place, notice
- **派生词**: spotlight (n.), spotted (adj.), spotless (adj.)

## spread
- **音标**: /spred/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 传播；展开；蔓延
- **例句**: The news spread quickly across the country.
- **近义词**: extend, expand, disseminate
- **派生词**: spreading (adj.)

## squeeze
- **音标**: /skwiːz/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 挤；压缩；榨取
- **例句**: He squeezed the toothpaste tube to get the last bit out.
- **近义词**: press, compress, crush
- **派生词**: squeezing (n.)

## stable
- **音标**: /ˈsteɪbl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 稳定的；马厩
- **例句**: The patient's condition is now stable.
- **近义词**: steady, secure, firm
- **派生词**: stability (n.), stabilize (v.), unstable (adj.)

## staff
- **音标**: /stæf/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 全体职员；工作人员
- **例句**: The company has a staff of 200 people.
- **近义词**: employees, workforce, personnel
- **派生词**: staffing (n.)
